Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:15:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] serve: CPU replay of the Genesis request shapes through
 the 90f73293 parser and this one

serve/test_genesis_shapes_replay.py feeds plausible model outputs for Genesis' four request shapes (helper without
thinking, json_object, agent with get_time and reasoning_effort low/xhigh, follow-up without a tool role) plus
file/shell tool calls whose values hold markdown fences (also nested) and literal </parameter> text through the
production parser (read from git, 90f73293:serve/frontend.py) and this tree's: streamed tool arguments on and off,
recovery on and off, whole and in 9 delta splits, ended by stop and by max_tokens (1728 runs). All events are
identical once a call's consecutive tool_args pieces are joined, and piece for piece with token-like deltas; the
only regrouping (12 runs, 64-character deltas) is 77794e34 holding the arguments until a following
<parameter=NAME> is complete. Also checks the request side (openai_to_messages, rendered prompt, e69cbfa5's
default-effort fill) is unchanged for the shapes, and that a value quoting a whole call - the intended
difference - is now exact where 90f73293 cut it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
